virglrenderer: patch varyings without a location on desktop GL (#589)

What: on desktop GL a patch varying gets no layout location, its name is zero-padded
(patch00, patch01 ... patch10 instead of patch0 ... patch10), and between a separable
tessellation control shader and a separable evaluation shader each one declares every patch
varying from 0 up to the highest one it declares (the control shader leaves the extra ones
unwritten, the evaluation shader does not read them). The shader key says whether the stage
before or after a separable shader is separable too (separable_in, separable_out, set in
vrend_sync_shader_io beside the masks a whole neighbour fills in). GLES keeps vrend's
locations and names.
Why: Apple's GL refuses any layout location on a patch variable ("Or active varying aliasing.
One or more slots starting at 0 unavailable for 'patch0' from layout location request"), so
every separable pipeline with a patch varying was refused and its draws skipped. Without a
location it gives the patch varyings of separate programs their slots in the order of their
names, not by name: an evaluation shader that declares only patch1 read the control shader's
patch0, and patch10 sorted before patch2. With zero-padded names and every patch varying from
0 declared in both stages, the n-th name is patch n in both. Seen alike on Apple's software
renderer and the M4 and M1 GPUs (macOS 27). Without a location GL matches by name (GL 4.1,
7.4.1), so the rule holds on any desktop GL; a separable stage next to a whole one is linked
into one program with it, and that link matches by name (the key masks give both the same
patch varyings, as for whole programs).
Upstream: not sent; virglrenderer main gives separable patch varyings the same locations
(checked 2026-10-31).
Test: Tests/virgl/test-separable-pervertex.c: separable pipelines with patch varyings on
Apple's software renderer: one patch varying (white), the evaluation shader reading one of
two (D1) or both (D2), patch varyings 1 and 3 beside a per-vertex varying (D4), twelve patch
varyings read at 2 and 10 (D6); each was refused before. One program of a separable and a
whole tessellation stage (M1, M2): drawn right or refused, never drawn wrong.

